    "title": "Pennsylvania State Police helicopter violently collides with plane, pilot dead: FAA - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Lindenmuth ,\n1 hours ago\nCARLISLE, Pa. ( WHTM ) -- An airplane and Pennsylvania State Police helicopter collided violently at the Carlisle Airport located in South Middleton Township, Pennsylvania, Wednesday evening, federal authorities confirmed to Nexstar's WHTM.\nTwo people were aboard the PSP aircraft when it collided midair with a Cessna 150 around 6:50 p.m., a Federal Aviation Administration spokesperson said in a statement. The plane was descending onto the runway\nGovernor Josh Shapiro said he had been briefed on the crash is en route.\n\"Lori and I are praying hard and we ask all of our fellow Pennsylvanians to join us,\" he said.\nPhoto Courtesy / Jamie Luster Photo Courtesy / Jamie Luster Photo Courtesy / Brandi Freet The number of people on board the airplane is not yet known.\nThe NTSB will lead an investigation along with the FAA, and has two NTSB investigators are en route to the site, the agency confirmed to WHTM News.\n\"After the wreckage is documented, it will be moved to a secure facility for further examination,\" an NTSB spokesperson said. \"Anyone with information that could be relevant to the investigation is asked to contact the NTSB at witness@ntsb.gov .\"\nCumberland County Coroner Charles Hall confirmed his office responded to the scene. Further details on any injuries remain few.\nPhotos and video sent to WHTM/abc27 News showed a State Police helicopter damaged and on its side in the grass alongside the runway.\nThe runway remains closed to fixed wing aircraft, according to an FAA Notice to Air Missions.\nWHTM has a crew at the scene and is working to learn more.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WETM - MyTwinTiers.com.",
    "summary": "CARLISLE, Pa. ( WHTM ) -- An airplane and Pennsylvania State Police helicopter collided violently at the Carlisle Airport located in South Middleton Township, Pennsylvania, Wednesday evening, federal authorities confirmed to Nexstar's WHTM. Two people were aboard the PSP aircraft when it collided midair with a Cessna 150 around 6:50 p.m., a Federal Aviation Administration spokesperson said in a statement. The plane was descending onto the runway Governor Josh Shapiro said he had been briefed on the crash is en route.",
